# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore for the public TRDFormer repository
#
# Two goals, which pull in opposite directions:
#   1. the clone must stay small enough to be useful (the working tree is
#      ~590 MB, of which 511 MB is per-sample prediction arrays);
#   2. it must still REPRODUCE every table and every metric figure in the
#      paper, which means the aggregate run records have to be tracked.
#
# The previous version of this file failed (2) by ignoring outputs/runs/ and
# outputs/manifests/ wholesale and by ignoring *.pkl globally -- that dropped
# run_records.jsonl and scaler.pkl, i.e. exactly the inputs the figure
# scripts read. The rules below therefore exclude by FILE PATTERN, not by
# directory, and add explicit negations where a broad rule would otherwise
# swallow something needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── Third-party data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SDWPF is a public dataset but redistribution terms are the publisher's, not
# ours. scripts/ contains the download + cleaning path instead; see README.
data/

# ── Manuscript sources ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The article is under review; the repository is a code and results deposit.
manuscript/

# ── Bulk experiment artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# 917 per-sample prediction arrays, ~511 MB. Regenerable by re-running the
# experiments; also available on request. Everything else under outputs/
# (run_records.jsonl, *_losses.npz, configs, manifests) is small and tracked.
outputs/**/*_preds.npz
outputs/manifests/vmd_imfs_causal_backup.npz
model_save/

# ── Checkpoints and binaries ───────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pt
*.pth
*.pkl
!outputs/manifests/scaler.pkl
tools/tectonic/

# ── Internal working notes (Chinese drafts, superseded claims) ─────────────
# Kept locally, not published: these predate the final manuscript and still
# assert things it retracted (e.g. a "strictly causal" DWT), so shipping them
# would contradict the paper.
论文*.md
论文*.pdf
LaTeX排版避坑文档.md
投稿材料清单.md
docs/
_cleanup_archive/
legacy/

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# ── Virtual environments ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
env/
ENV/
.venv/

# ── Optuna / databases ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/

# ── IDE / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Scratch files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ad-hoc debug scripts accumulated at the repo root during troubleshooting
# (_debug_full.*, _bisect*.py, _mini.*, pandoc_log*.txt were all found there
# in the 2026-08 cleanup), so anything root-level starting with an underscore
# is ignored.
*.tmp
*.bak
/_*
pandoc_log*.txt
/*.aux
/*.bbl
/*.blg
/*.out
/*.toc
/*.fls
/*.fdb_latexmk
